 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-002\", \"clauses\": {\"present_data\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"Make a picture graph to show: {data_str}. Draw one {symbol} for each item.\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 is a question_text family whose task is to make a graph from given data. Its data_str slot is filled by F09 from the _THEMES row and its symbol slot from the same row, so the learner is asked to present data.\"}, \"pictograph\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"Make a picture graph to show: {data_str}. Draw one {symbol} for each item.\", \"reasoning\": \"The question asks the learner to build a picture graph in which each count is shown by repeated symbols, which is the pictograph representation. The word pictograph itself is printed only in hint F04 via F01, so the representation is carried by F07's picture graph wording.\"}, \"without_scale\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"Each picture stands for 1 item.\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 states the one-to-one unit of the graph, so each picture counts as exactly one item and no scale is needed. The declared bound no_scale is consistent with this text, and the F07 instruction to draw one symbol for each item reinforces it in the question.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [], \"failing_templates\": [], \"overall\": \"PASS\", \"reasoning\": \"Every family is grade 1 readable and uses only words in cumulative_vocab or the introduced vocabulary (pictograph, data, picture graph is not in NOT_YET_KNOWN, survey is not in NOT_YET_KNOWN). No family prints a NOT_YET_KNOWN term. The only nested learner text, F09 through F05 to F08, prints a category from the _THEMES row with a count from 1 to 5, which is in range and uses no commas. The symbol and categories come from the same row because one_row_per_problem is true. The hint F04 prints the word pictograph, which is in introduces_vocab. The one weakness is that F09 prints a single category